-- title:
--   Enlarging a finitely generated subring into a given open locus
-- statement:
--   Let $S$ be a commutative ring, let $S_0 \subseteq S$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra which is finitely generated (in the sense that $S_0$ is the $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra generated by a finite subset of $S$), and let $U \subseteq \operatorname{Spec} S_0$ be an open subset such that for every prime $p$ of $S$ the image of $p$ under the map $\operatorname{Spec} S \to \operatorname{Spec} S_0$ induced by the inclusion $S_0 \hookrightarrow S$ lies in $U$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra $S_1$ of $S$ together with an inclusion $S_0 \le S_1$ such that $S_1$ is again finitely generated as a $\mathbb{Z}$-algebra, and such that for every prime $q$ of $S_1$ the image of $q$ under the map $\operatorname{Spec} S_1 \to \operatorname{Spec} S_0$ induced by the inclusion ring homomorphism $S_0 \hookrightarrow S_1$ lies in $U$. Thus the hypothesis that the whole of $\operatorname{Spec} S$ maps into $U$ is already witnessed by a finitely generated intermediate subalgebra.
--
--   This is the refinement step of the standard "spreading out" argument: a condition that holds over the full ring $S$ already holds over some finitely generated subring containing a given one. It is used in the construction of a group law on a Jacobian over an arbitrary base, via [`GoodReductionJacobian.exists_relativeGroupLaw_one_eq_and_isCommutative_of_forall_abelian_geometricFibre`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.exists_relativeGroupLaw_one_eq_and_isCommutative_of_forall_abelian_geometricFibre).
